# How I Became Christian (Part 3)
## My journey from initial belief to that rare peace I'd seen in others

*Read part one [here](HOME_URL_PHhow-i-became-christian-1/).*
*Read part two [here](HOME_URL_PHhow-i-became-christian-2/).*

[describe the next seven years of continuing to learn and doubt etc etc, including realization about JW doctrine being pretty sound, more aligned with me on many points eg hell, and 'fruits', persecution, etc. Leading to deep investigation of JW... I'd always said you take the whole truth, you don't get to pick and choose the parts you like, truth doesn't work that way. Include previous investigation of other denoms, Catholic (is it true? Then marriage weirdness will have to ensue), Calvinism, etc. and why I rejected each one. Include stumbling across claims that Paul usurped the early church, and realizing it was not true because of the love poem. Etc.]

 And I am so, so grateful every day to God, who calls me to do better even as he loves me without reserve. I belong entirely to him now. Every day I lay my faults and failures at his feet, and every day he shapes me just a little more into the person he made me to be. It isn't that he changes me, I think; it's that he cleans me, wipes off the grime of my lifelong attempts to run my life myself, so that more of his love courses through me in the way he intended. Sometimes the grime is crusted tight, and the cleaning is hard to take; even then, I know I am his treasured child, and I am eager to delight him. The reins of my life are in his hands, where they belong, and I have never felt more seen, heard and understood.